<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Quarkus + LangChain4j — DEPENDENCY REFERENCE (this is NOT a full pom.xml).

  The project SHELL — the full pom.xml: the quarkus-bom + quarkus-langchain4j-bom platform BOMs,
  the build plugins, the `-parameters` compiler flag (parameter-name retention), the `native`
  profile, the test stack, and every version pin — is generated, already up to date, by the
  Quarkus Agents MCP `quarkus_create` (the same codestart generator that powers code.quarkus.io).
  It is intentionally NOT hand-maintained here: a pinned copy only drifts (in v0.5.0 the baseline
  had already fallen behind the live platform).

  So this file keeps only the two things a project generator does NOT give you.

  ==========================================================================
  1. Extensions to pass to quarkus_create (resolved against the current platform BOM)
  ==========================================================================
    core:    rest, rest-jackson, smallrye-openapi, websockets-next, langchain4j-ollama
    agents:  + langchain4j-agentic     (declarative LangChain4j Agentic workflows)
    RAG:     + langchain4j-easy-rag     (Easy RAG)
    MCP client: + langchain4j-mcp      (consume tools from remote MCP servers)
    MCP server: + mcp-server-http      (expose this app as an MCP server; stdio variant: mcp-server-stdio)
    observability: + micrometer-registry-prometheus, opentelemetry   (optional; see application.properties.template)
    fault tolerance: + smallrye-fault-tolerance                      (optional; MicroProfile FT on AI-service methods)
    error contract: + http-problem     (optional; io.quarkiverse.httpproblem; RFC 9457 problem+json at the REST edge)
    agent skills:   + langchain4j-skills   (optional; loads SKILL.md-format skills at runtime; status:preview)

  All of the above are platform extensions: quarkus_create resolves them and the BOMs manage
  their versions, so none of them belongs in the <dependencies> below and none takes a <version>.
  (http-problem joined io.quarkus.platform:quarkus-bom in 3.38.0 — the extension's own README
  still says otherwise, but the BOM on Maven Central is authoritative.)

  quarkus-arc, quarkus-junit and rest-assured are pulled in automatically — do not list them.

  ==========================================================================
  2. Non-extension dependencies the generator does NOT add — paste into <dependencies>
  ==========================================================================
  Most live under the dev.langchain4j group (they are libraries, not Quarkus extensions); the
  test-scoped eval artifact is a quarkiverse module the generator likewise omits. Neither
  quarkus_create nor code.quarkus.io will add any of them, and their versions are managed by
  quarkus-langchain4j-bom, so they take NO <version>. Add each only when its feature is used
  (output guardrails, RAG embedding model, PDF parsing, AI-quality evals).
-->
<dependencies>

    <!-- agents: CompleteAnswerGuard extends dev.langchain4j.guardrails.JsonExtractorOutputGuardrail
         (the copy in langchain4j-core is deprecated for removal and gone from LangChain4j 1.20) -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>dev.langchain4j</groupId>
        <artifactId>langchain4j-guardrails</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- RAG: in-process embedding model required by Easy RAG -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>dev.langchain4j</groupId>
        <artifactId>langchain4j-embeddings-bge-small-en-v15-q</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- RAG: add only if ingesting PDFs -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>dev.langchain4j</groupId>
        <artifactId>langchain4j-document-parser-apache-pdfbox</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- testing: AI-quality evals (Scorer/@EvaluationTest) -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>io.quarkiverse.langchain4j</groupId>
        <artifactId>quarkus-langchain4j-testing-evaluation-junit5</artifactId>
        <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>

</dependencies>
